Routal runs on Talos Linux (https://github.com/siderolabs/talos, Copyright (c)
Sidero Labs, Inc., MPL-2.0). It does not include Talos source code.

The extension image bundles unmodified Alpine Linux packages and their libraries,
run as separate programs: nftables (GPL-2.0), Kea (MPL-2.0), Unbound
(BSD-3-Clause), radvd (BSD-style), chrony (GPL-2.0) and Avahi (LGPL-2.1). Their
sources are available from https://pkgs.alpinelinux.org and the upstream projects.
Also: ppp (BSD-style and GPL-2.0 parts), rp-pppoe (GPL-2.0) and inadyn (GPL-2.0).

It also bundles miniupnpd (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) Thomas Bernard), built
unmodified from https://github.com/miniupnp/miniupnp with its nftables backend.

routald includes these Go modules: gopkg.in/yaml.v3 (MIT and Apache-2.0),
github.com/insomniacslk/dhcp (BSD-3-Clause), github.com/vishvananda/netlink and
github.com/vishvananda/netns (Apache-2.0), golang.org/x/sys (BSD-3-Clause), and their
dependencies; their licenses are in their sources.
